    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\n### Description\nWhen using the `:set wrap` option in Neovim, the reference line wraps correctly, but the virtual line drawn above the reference line does not wrap accordingly. This leads to a visual mismatch where the virtual line appears out of sync with the wrapped reference line.\n\n### Expected Behavior\nThe virtual line above the reference line should wrap in sync with the wrapped reference line when line wrapping is enabled.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n1. Open a file containing a long text that exceeds the width of the Neovim window.\n2. Enable line wrapping via `:set wrap` in Neovim.\n3. Toggle the diff overlay functionaliy `MiniDiff.toggle_overlay()`\n4. Modify the reference line.\n5. Observe that the virtual line drawn above the reference line does not wrap with it.\n",
