        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nUnfortunately, there is very little 'mini.diff' can do here. The overlay functionality uses virtual lines which does not support autowrapping. It [might be planned](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18282#issuecomment-2667771187) but it is not currently implemented. In fact, virtual lines didn't even support horizontal scrolling until Neovim=0.11 (i.e. `virt_lines_overflow='scroll'`).\n\n*In theory* it might be possible to 1) splice virtual line into several lines depending on the wrap; or 2) autoinsert inline text inside buffer line to mimic wrapped virtual lines. Both of these approach are a bit crazy and will be very complex *and* fragile.\n\nSo I am going to close this as \"not (reasonably) possible until Neovim implements necessary functionality\".",
